From b844282f85f8062299ba5acd6aa0eb59fd73f02c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:33:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0194 launcher: V1.3.40 redesign - poster + glass box + icon
 bar + in-box character picker

The launcher main screen is rebuilt around the user-approved mockup
(launcher-mockup-charbox.png): the Odyssey poster stays full-bleed on
the left with the title and the red Start button; the right ~60% is one
liquid-glass box showing the active tab's content; the bottom bar is a
narrow centred pill of 6 large icons only (game / controls / performance /
data / cloud / character), the active one red. Nothing opens full-screen
any more - 0185's fullScreenCover is gone, the settings groups (all 16
rows + game data + cloud saves) render inside the box, scrollable.

One glass-intensity setting (UserDefaults DmGlassOpacity, 0-100,
default 70) drives both the box and the bottom bar; iOS 26 uses native
.glassEffect, below it ultraThinMaterial. The slider lives at the top of
the Game tab.

The character picker moves into the box: hero on the left, a flat
stacked outfit deck on the right (front card gold-bordered with an
animated holographic foil, two back cards peeking up-right; swipe the
front card to cycle, tap to select), 6 character cards along the bottom.
Mario gets all 50 caps + 52 clothes; Luigi his 3 clothes + default cap;
Wario his 8 icon'd costumes per slot; Peach / Pauline / Toad default only
for now. Outfit cards show the game's real 8-bit dot-art icons (67 PNGs
bundled in LauncherBackground, referenced as outfit_<ItemName>); the
hero and cards use the char_<id>.png renders. WarioCaptain / WarioHigh /
Luigi caps have no dot-art file in RomFS and are not offered.

Swift cannot compile on this host (no Xcode/iOS toolchain) - the only
compile check is CI. The file was re-read top to bottom; every
if/else in a View body is Group-wrapped, every UIImage(named:) name was
script-checked against the bundled files (71 names, 0 missing).
